{"t": 1794116420.9463227, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Main pipeline #8812 is red \u2014 root cause and fix**\n\nThe `test:contract` job failed with:\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing.invoice.invoice_number()` interpolated the raw integer sequence, so invoice numbers came out as `INV-2026-42`. The contract test (`contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits for the Finance ERP import (FIN-77).\n\nFix applied in `billing/invoice.py`:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerification (matching the contract case and edge cases):\n- `invoice_number(2026, 42)` -> `INV-2026-000042` (contract test passes)\n- `invoice_number(2026, 7)` -> `INV-2026-000007`\n- `invoice_number(2025, 999999)` -> `INV-2025-999999` (6 digits unchanged)\n- sequences longer than 6 digits are not truncated (`1000000` -> `INV-2026-1000000`)\n\nNote for this MR: the ERP v2 format change must keep the 6-digit zero-padded sequence, otherwise the Finance ERP import contract (FIN-77) will fail again.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
